#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# acoth

#% text
# `acoth(z)` gives the inverse hyperbolic cotangent.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `atanh(1/z)`.

#% item
# Exact special values and odd symmetry are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
acoth(0)
#% output
#= complex(0, 1/2)*pi

#% cell
acoth(2.0)
#% output
#= 0.5493061443340549

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
acoth(0.5)
#% output
#= complex(0.5493061443340549, -1.5707963267948966)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(acoth(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= complex(0.346573590279972654708616060729088, -1.570796326794896619231321691639751)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
